# Backend (Goat OS)

Read **`backend/AGENTS.md`** and the build skill reference
`.agents/skills/goatos-build/references/backend-impl.md` before editing.

## Non-negotiables

- Handlers thin; domain logic inside modules; module-owned tables only.
- Million-goat scale: tenant/run scoped, indexed, paginated/keyset reads — no
  full-herd API scans.
- Idempotency on every mutating path; tests for first call, exact replay, and
  same-key different-payload replay.
- Observability via `backend/internal/platform/observability` — no hand-rolled
  `slog.New` in new code.
- sqlc + goose migrations; validate hot-path query plans when touching large tables.

## Local API

Starting bare `go run ./cmd/api` without env fails. Use `make dev-local` or:

```bash
export GOATOS_ENV=local GOATOS_AUTH_MODE=bearer \
  GOATOS_AUTH_HS256_SECRET=goatos-local-dev-secret-32-bytes-min \
  GOATOS_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080 \
  DATABASE_URL='postgres://postgres:goatos@127.0.0.1:5432/goatos?sslmode=disable'
cd backend && go run ./cmd/api
```

Keep API (`:8080`) and admin-web (`:3300`) as separate long-lived processes.
